abstract: >-
  A practical Quality Engineering framework for using large language models as
  semantic evaluators while treating the judge itself as a measurement system
  that must be calibrated, versioned, tested and governed. The work covers
  deterministic-first evaluation, rubric engineering, human calibration,
  repeated-run stability, position and style bias, cross-judge agreement,
  uncertainty, false-pass control, adversarial judge testing, judge regression,
  observability, cost, CI/CD quality gates and continuous meta-evaluation.